+    11	A fresh run records actual adapter calls. Replay checks each artifact digest,
+    12	validates the stage roster and re-derives the report using its retained
+    13	response table and the independent producer pin.
+    14	The replay path invokes the local GND verifiers and performs zero producer
+    15	calls. It exits 3 with incomplete status if a required artifact is stale,
+    16	missing or differs on re-derivation.
+    17	
+    18	## Stage files
+    19	
+    20	The independent input roster names source versions, document digests,
+    21	section identifiers and byte spans. Available section, table and equation
+    22	entries can be inventoried. The stage files occur in this order.
+    23	
+    24	1. Inventory
+    25	2. Broad extraction
+    26	3. Targeted selection
+    27	4. Targeted extraction
+    28	5. Review
+    29	6. Affected recheck
+    30	
+    31	Each `stage-N.json` binds the exact input digests, predecessor record and
+    32	corresponding `payload-N.json`. The saved attempt rows bind the selected
+    33	source range and producer response. The review payload binds its separate
+    34	source judgments and the targeted vocabulary proposal that produces a revisit
+    35	list of previously inspected sections. The run manifest binds all stage and
+    36	companion artifacts. A targeted pass recovers a fact from the methods note.
+    37	A separate synthetic source excerpt reports both conflicting labels. The
+    38	saved candidate binds those labels to the excerpt and fails public verify
+    39	and check.
