e LR1-C1 test as planned would hit exit 3 on the packaged fixture."}],"recommendation":"Add one line to the plan (§2 LR1 or §3 Fixtures) stating that the documented steps and the LR1 test must stage the model with its include — `reading.orm.json` beside `vocabulary.orm.json`, run from that folder — so the page and LR1-C1 are measurable as written.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR1's documented verify steps omit the model-include staging the probe requires"},{"concern_id":"lr2r2-path-prefix","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"H8 line 101, H9 line 102, H11 line 104, H13 line 106, H15 line 108, H16 line 109, H21 line 114","observation":"The plan cites `examples/literature/reading.py:176-193`, `reading.py:390-392`, `reading.py:93-112`, `reading.py:42`, `:311-341`, `:149-158`, `:562-584`, `:587-596` and `examples/literature/README.md`, but the tracked paths are `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py` and `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md` (§3 line 196 and §5 already use the full prefix). The line numbers themselves are correct under the real path — e.g. `reading.py:390-392` is exactly `document = b\"\\n\".join(inputs.source_range(inputs.sections[row[\"section\"]]) for row in attempts)` — so this is a citation-prefix inconsistency, not a wrong claim."}],"recommendation":"Normalize the abbreviated `examples/literature/…` prefixes in H8-H16 and H21 to `src/gnd/examples/literature/…` so every citation resolves unambiguously.","relevance":"completeness","severity":"low","title":"Several H-row path citations drop the src/gnd/ prefix"},{"concern_id":"lr2r2-h22-lint-staleness","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"H22 line 115","observation":"H22 states \"whole-repository `uv run ruff check` exits 1 on files dev-tools delivers; `uv run ruff check