erence-plan.md","location":"§10, open questions carried into the specs","observation":"\"LR1, whether the page's steps are shown as a short Python snippet the documentation tests run or as prose with field names\" - the plan leaves the page's form open, so \"the test reads the page\" has no defined way to enumerate \"every field name the page uses\"."}],"recommendation":"Widen LR1-C3 to cover both report-level and verdict-level names (or state which level the page may use), and fix the identifier convention the test extracts (for example: every backticked identifier in the \"Reading a failed verification\" section), either in the plan or as a decision the LR1 spec must record at its gate.","relevance":"blocking","severity":"medium","title":"LR1-C3 is unsatisfiable as written: it checks page field names against the verdict only, while §2/H2/H6 require report-level names, and the extraction rule is left open"},{"concern_id":"lr1-c4-fixtures-not-named","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§4 LR1-C4","observation":"\"**LR1-C4** a deontic-only violation is listed as a warning and not as a failure; a redacting model gives the marker and the page says so.\" - the criterion requires two situations beyond a failing alethic verdict."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§3, Fixtures","observation":"\"LR1 uses the packaged reading run's reported conflict (`reported-conflict.population.json`, which the example already verifies at exit 1) and its broad population (exit 0).\" - only two fixtures are named; no deontic-only source and no redacting-model case appear, and §9's LR1 lane adds no fixture file."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§1 H5","observation":"The redaction behaviour is the one row the plan did not run: \"when a model's redaction policy selects a verdict's roles, `message` becomes a fixed marker and `offending_facts` one marker row\", kind \"observed by reading\"."}],"recommendation":"In §3 (or as a required LR1 spec decision) name where the deontic-only and redacted verdicts come from - for example reusing the cases H20 cites at `tests/test_verify_cli.py:309-336`, `:387` for the deontic side, and a stated redaction policy plus source for the H5 side - so LR1-C4 is testable within the fixtures the plan provides.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR1-C4 requires deontic-only and redacted-verdict cases that §3's fixture list does not provide, and H5 was never run"},{"concern_id":"lr2-index-passage-claim-unreconciled","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§1 H21","observation":"\"`index.md:11` says \"GND keeps each claim tied to its passage\"; none states where a quote may lie\" - the plan records a literature-page sentence asserting a claim-to-passage tie."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§10 D2 (b) and §2 LR2","observation":"D2 (b) proposes \"A quote may lie anywhere in the document the sidecar names, and the pages recommend naming the whole source version and recording the section\", and §2 states \"GND has no notion of the section a model was shown.\" - the quoted `index.md:11` sentence asserts the opposite tie."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§4 LR2-C1..C4 and §3 LR2 homes","observation":"§3 lists `docs/literature/index.md` as an LR2 home, but the criteria require only \"**LR2-C1** the rule is stated once, in `anchors.md`, and the literature pages cite it\", plus the two binding outcomes and byte identity - none requires the passage-tie sentence to be corrected, although §6 names the misreading as a risk: \"A host reads \"anywhere in the document\" as \"any text is evidence\"\"."}],"recommendation":"Add to LR2-C1 (or a new LR2 criterion) that the literature pages stop asserting a claim-to-passage tie that D2 (b) contradicts, and name `docs/literature/index.md:11` as the line the phase reconciles, so the page the plan already quotes does not survive as a counter-statement of the rule.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR2 leaves `docs/literature/index.md:11`'s \"GND keeps each claim tied to its passage\" standing against D2 (b), with no criterion covering it"},{"concern_id":"lr2-c1-no-verification-mechanism","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§4 LR2-C1","observation":"\"**LR2-C1** the rule is stated once, in `anchors.md`, and the literature pages cite it.\" - a documentation criterion with no stated holder."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§2 LR2, test bullet","observation":"\"A test pins both sides with one source and one quote from its second section: bound when the document is the whole source, refused with `anchor:binding-mismatch` when the document is the first section.\" - the only LR2 test described checks binding behaviour, not the pages."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§9, LR1 and LR2 lanes","observation":"LR1's lane names a documentation test (\"`uv run pytest -q tests/test_lr1_verify_failure_listing.py tests/test_verify_cli.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_documentation_tutorials.py --tb=short`\") and §2 LR1 says its test \"fails if the page names a field the report does not carry\"; LR2's lane is \"`uv run pytest -q tests/test_lr2_quote_scope.py tests/test_anchor_sidecar_v2.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py --tb=short`\", with no documentation test."}],"recommendation":"State which artifact holds LR2-C1 - either add a documentation test to the LR2 lane (mirroring LR1's `tests/test_documentation_tutorials.py` and the \"test reads the page\" pattern), extend `tests/test_lr2_quote_scope.py` to assert the single statement in `anchors.md` and the citations from the literature pages, or mark C1 as an owner-gate manual check.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR2-C1 has no named verification mechanism: §2's LR2 test pins only binding behaviour and §9's LR2 lane names no documentation test"},{"concern_id":"lr2-example-readme-home-without-criterion","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§3, LR2 homes","observation":"\"`docs/reference/anchors.md`, `docs/literature/index.md`, `docs/literature/commands.md`, `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md`, a new `tests/test_lr2_quote_scope.py`, `docs/release-notes.md`\" - the example's README is a changed home."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§1 H9 and §7","observation":"H9: \"the document the example hands to `gnd verify` is the shown sections joined with newlines, not the declared source. The example writes no anchor sidecar\"; §7 keeps it that way: \"A quote or claim concept in the reading example. It has none today (H8) and LR2 documents the anchor rule without adding one.\" - the shipped example therefore does what §2 LR2 recommends against (\"the pages recommend the whole source version\")."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§4 LR2 criteria","observation":"LR2-C1 to LR2-C4 cover the rule's single home, the two binding outcomes and byte identity of the packaged 