eld names only against \"the verdict\" although section 2 with H2 and H6 requires the page to name report-level fields (`outcome`, `counts.fail`, exit 1) - as written LR1 would fail its own criterion or have it silently narrowed. Hardening: LR1-C4's deontic and redacted cases have no fixture in section 3; the H2-H4 probe is written as `MODEL POP` so the LR1 baseline cannot be re-run from the plan; `docs/literature/index.md:11`'s \"tied to its passage\" claim is left unreconciled with D2 (b); LR2-C1 has no named verification mechanism; the LR2 home `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md` carries no criterion while section 7 keeps H9's counterexample; D9's per-stage prompts conflict with H16 and section 3's reading.py limit. Completeness: the writer-conflict sentence and LR1's homes disagree about `index.md`, and D5 shipping LR1/LR2 ahead leaves #226 with no reply until a close that waits on another milestone."},"response_salvage":{"complete":true,"declared_concern_count":11,"dropped":[],"dropped_overflow":0,"preamble_lines":0,"retained_concern_count":11,"trailing_lines":0,"transport":"jsonl"},"reviewer_id":"qwen","schema_version":1,"status":"success"}
