d and the rows that violate each'. No criterion covers a derivation failure or requires that an exit-1 report gives a non-empty listing. LR1-C1 to C4 cover only a uniqueness failure, a pass, a deontic warning and a redacted verdict."}],"recommendation":"Have the page's steps also read failing `derivations`, or at least say that exit 1 can come from them and what they carry. Add a criterion that every exit-1 fixture gives a non-empty listing, and one derivation-failure case to the LR1 test.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR1's documented steps miss exit-1 failures that come from derivation verdicts"},{"concern_id":"d4-span-overlap-has-no-fact-span","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 10 D4, line 318","observation":"D4 proposes 'Span overlap plus participant names, as #226 scored, so the figures are comparable; predicate agreement reported beside it'."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 1 H8, line 101; section 7, line 262","observation":"H8 says 'a producer response is `{outcome, facts, proposal_keys}`. There is no quote in it and no check of one'. Section 7 puts out of scope 'A quote or claim concept in the reading example. It has none today (H8)'. reading.py:176-193 records only the section's `start` and `end` for each attempt, so a produced fact's only span is its whole section. D4's span overlap would then measure section overlap, not the quote-level overlap #226 scored. That defeats D4's stated reason ('so the figures are comparable'), unless LR3 adds the quote concept that section 7 excludes."}],"recommendation":"State in D4 which span a produced fact is scored by: its section span, or a span LH1 adds. Qualify or drop the comparability claim to match. Or move the question of a quote concept into D9 or LR3's spec gate, and say so.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"D4's span-overlap scoring rule has no per-fact span in the reading output"},{"concern_id":"d8-home-outside-packaged-skill","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 10 D8, line 322; section 5, lines 233-235","observation":"D8 proposes '(a); the other two cite it', where (a) is `docs/guides/documents.md`. Section 5 says '`gnd-extract`'s `extraction-contract.md` gains one citing line; its manifest is held by `tests/test_packaged_skills.py`'. tests/test_packaged_skills.py:101-125 fails on any relative link from a skill file that does not resolve inside the packaged skills tree, and src/gnd/skills/gnd-extract/references/extraction-contract.md has no absolute URL today. The agent that follows that contract's 'REPORT IT' row (line 145) has only the installed skill, not docs/."}],"recommendation":"Say how the skill cites the docs home: an absolute repository URL, or a short summary of the field names inside the skill with the docs page as the full home. Either way, the agent that hits exit 1 under gnd-extract can follow the citation, and the packaged-skill link guard stays green.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"low","title":"The packaged gnd-extract contract cannot link to a docs/ home by relative path"},{"concern_id":"lr2-example-document-mischaracterized","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 2 LR2, lines 170-173","observation":"The plan says 'If the host verifies against the shown section only, as the packaged reading example does (H9), a quote from elsewhere cannot bind.' and adds that 'the pages recommend the whole source version'."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 1 H9, line 102","observation":