+# Panel Review
+## Summary
+Second and final round, over plan r3. Three of six seats succeeded \(Claude, Codex, GLM\), exactly the quorum; Qwen timed out, Gemini and Kimi returned no schema-valid response. All three voted revise and none raised a blocking concern. Claude and GLM found all seven round-one fixes resolved; Codex found five resolved and two incomplete. Three concerns reached agreement: the interim \#226 reply has no LR2 home \(Claude, Codex, GLM\); the example&\#x27;s second verify path and its extraction sidecar are missing from H9 and LR2-C5 \(Claude, Codex\); D1 \(d\)&\#x27;s &\#x27;extend&\#x27; contradicts R0.4 and the LR3 lane omits the corpus tests \(Claude, GLM\). The driving agent confirmed the conflict path \(reading.py:395\), the disclosure table \(docs/reference/disclosure.md:20\) and the corpus tests&\#x27; existence. Claude and GLM share one CLI codebase, so two of the three successes are weaker evidence of independence.
