literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§2 LR1, lines 157 and 160","observation":"r3 adds \"are the `derivations` with `verdict: \"fail\"` (H23)\" and \"A failing derivation names itself by `derivation_ref`\", followed by `findings`. In src/gnd/report.schema.json, `derivation_ref` and `findings` are properties of the `derivation_verdict*` definitions, not the constraint `verdict*` definitions (`verdict_v10` holds constraint_ref, offending_facts and the rest). The two packaged sources have no failing derivation. So 'verdict level' and 'the live report' do not say where these names are checked. The code spans that §2 models the section on also hold values (`\"fail\"`, `warning`, `uniqueness`), which are not field names."}],"recommendation":"State LR1-C3 over three levels: report, constraint verdict and derivation verdict. Check each against its schema definition and against the live report of the fixture that carries it; derivation fields come from the authored derivation failure. Say how the test separates field names from values in code spans, for example with a listed set of names or a marked syntax.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"low","title":"LR1-C3 does not cover the derivation-verdict fields r3 adds to the page"},{"concern_id":"issue-reply-timing-split","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§10 D5, line 351","observation":"D5 adds \"`(r3)` An interim reply to #226 covering requests 3 and 2 is drafted when LR2 merges (`notes/issue-reply.md`); the owner posts it.\""},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"§5, line 268; §3 LR3 row, line 219; §11, line 378","observation":"§5 still reads \"- **Issue reply.** The close drafts it; the owner posts it.\". §3 lists `notes/issue-reply.md` only among LR3's homes. §11 gives the fix's si