+   136	## 5. Failure semantics
+   137	
+   138	| What happened | Machine-readable form | Exit | What you do |
+   139	|---|---|---|---|
+   140	| The population file does not parse | population fails to load | 3 | re-emit the whole file (§2); never hand-repair |
+   141	| The sidecar is absent | `extraction:sidecar-missing`, state `failed` | 3 | write it; absence is a FAILURE, never a skip |
+   142	| The sidecar has an unknown field, a missing digest, or an unsafe path | `extraction:sidecar-invalid`, state `failed` | 3 | fix the sidecar against §3 |
+   143	| A recorded digest does not match the file bytes | `extraction:binding-mismatch`, state `failed` | 3 | recompute digests after the last write and rewrite the sidecar |
+   144	| The header disagrees with the model | `extraction:header-mismatch`, state `failed` | 3 | re-copy `header_template` verbatim (§4) |
+   145	| The checker found an alethic violation | verdicts on the checker channel, state `ran` | 1 | REPORT IT — the document describes a world that violates the model |
+   146	| The population is vacuous | state `ran` | 2 | report it; a document that supports no facts is a finding |
+   147	| The checker could not decide | state `ran` | 4 | report it |
+   148	| Everything held | state `ran` | 0 | report it |
+   149	
+   150	The three states are `ran`, `skipped` and `failed`. **`skipped` is written only by the intentional opt-out `gnd verify --no-extraction`** — you never write it, and a missing file never produces it. A measurement that did not happen must not read as green.
+   151	
+   152	Exit 0 with state `ran` is **checker acceptance**, not proof of faithfulness. A hallucinated, well-shaped, conforming population exits 0. That is a real extractor error and it is exactly what `gnd fidelity` exists to measure; nothing in a `verify` payload speaks to it, and no rate ever appears there.
