l\n303\t\n304\t- `auto=true` `(r3)`: the owner delegated approval for this milestone on\n305\t  2026-11-23 (\"they should both start with /process-milestone auto\"). The\n306\t  plan gate, each spec gate and the close are ruled under that delegation\n307\t  and recorded as delegated rulings. It authorizes no paid producer call,\n308\t  no credential, no publication and no merge.\n309\t- Plan review and close review: the full GND panel (D6, the owner's ruling).\n310\t  Round one read r2 and blocked (Codex). The budget is two rounds; round two\n311\t  reads r3. Stop criterion, declared here before round two: after round two\n312\t  the plan is ruled on its findings with no third round; a blocking finding\n313\t  that survives reproduction is fixed and recorded at the gate.\n314\t- Phase-diff review: one independent reviewer in a different tool per phase\n315\t  (the owner's ruling, \"Review helper, both\") `(r3)`.\n316\t- The plan gate is recorded in `001-plan-gate.md` once the owner rules D1–D9\n317\t  or amends them.\n318\t- Each phase: spec, owner gate, change, focused gates, one independent\n319\t  reviewer over the diff, refactoring review, record, commit.\n320\t- LR3's live run is an owner-selected step inside its phase, with the\n321\t  producer and budget named in its spec (D3). Nothing in this plan\n322\t  authorizes it.\n323\t- One pull request from the topic branch to `main`, or two if LR1 and LR2\n324\t  merge ahead of LR3 (D5). Merge stays with the owner. Before the pull\n325\t  request, `python3 scripts/components_index.py changed --base origin/main --strict`\n326\t  exits 0.\n327\t\n328\t## 9. Per-phase verification\n329\t\n330\t| Phase | Focused lane | Expected |\n331\t|---|---|---|\n332\t| LR1 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lr1_verify_failure_listing.py tests/test_verify_cli.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_documentation_tutorials.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n333\t| LR2 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lr2_quote_scope.py tests/test_anchor_sidecar_v2.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n334\t| LR3 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lr3_reference_set.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py tests/test_ld5_verdict.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n335\t| all | the structure and inventory guard block of `project.md`, `uv run ruff check` `(r3)`, and `python3 scripts/components_index.py changed --base origin/main --strict` | exit 0 |\n336\t\n337\tThe lanes name files that exist at `548b9a1d`, plus one new file per phase.\n338\tAffected consumers are read again at each spec and may be widened there. No\n339\tbroad lane (`-m \"evidence or census\"`) is selected.\n340\t\n341\t## 10. Owner decisions and open questions\n342\t\n343\tAll rows are proposals until the plan gate rules them.\n344\t\n345\t| ID | Question | Proposed |\n346\t|---|---|---|\n347\t| D1 | LR3: the labelled set. (a) A small set written for the example from openly licensed papers. (b) The corpus run the literature-depth close carried (H18). (c) Ask the reporter for a redistributable slice of theirs. (d) `(r3)` Reuse or extend the packaged regression corpus and its answer key (H24) | (d) if LR3's spec shows the reading stages can read its documents as sources with sections; else (a). (b) stays carried `(r3)` |\n348\t| D2 | LR2: the rule. (a) A quote must lie inside the section the model was shown. (b) A quote may lie anywhere in the document the sidecar names, and the pages recommend naming the whole source version and recording the section | (b). It is what `bind_anchors` enforces today (H10); (a) would need a new check and a section concept GND does not have `(r2)` |\n349\t| D3 | LR3: the producer and its budget for the recorded run | Owner names one model and a ceiling; the run is recorded once and replayed after |\n350\t| D4 | LR3: the scoring rule for \"a gold fact is found\" | Participant names plus the section the fact was read from overlapping the gold passage, with predicate agreement reported beside it; the scorer reuses `assurance_report.py`'s precision and recall counting (H24). A produced fact has no span of its own (H8), only its section's, so the figures are comparable to #226's only at section grain, and the page says so. If LH1 adds a per-fact span, LR3's spec may score by it `(r3)` |\n351\t| D5 | Whether LR1 and LR2 ship ahead of LR3, by their own pull request | Yes `(r2)`. They need no other milestone, and LR3 waits for literature-host-interfaces. The outline proposed holding them so the three replies go out together; LR3 now waits for two phases of another milestone. `(r3)` An interim reply to #226 covering requests 3 and 2 is drafted when LR2 merges (`notes/issue-reply.md`); the owner posts it. If LH1 or LH2 is not on `main` when LR1 and LR2 close, LR3 waits and the milestone stays open; carrying LR3 is the owner's decision |\n352\t| D6 | Plan review and close review instrument | **Ruled by the owner, 2026-11-23: \"Full panel, both\"** `(o)`. The full GND panel for plan and close review. r2's proposal, superseded: \"the GND panel light for both\" |\n353\t| D7 `(r2)` | LR1: does `gnd verify` change. (a) No: the JSON report already answers the request and the phase is a page and a test. (b) (a), and the text output prints each failing verdict's rows under its line. (c) (a), and `gnd verify` accepts `--rule-ids` as `gnd check` does, so a verdict carries the constraint's declared id | (a). #226 asks for no format change (H19). (c) is the one that would let a host name a constraint by its id and not by position; it is offered, not proposed |\n354\t| D8 `(r2)` | LR1: the one home of \"Reading a failed verification\". (a) `docs/guides/documents.md`, after the verify command. (b) `extraction-contract.md` §5, in the packaged skill. (c) `docs/reference/cli.md` | (a); the other two cite it |\n355\t| D9 `(r2)` | LR3: what \"stage settings\" means, given that a run has only a budget and a scenario (H16) | The record names the producer, the budget and the roster's split into opening and targeted sections, read from the settings LH2 writes into a run, and the prompt of each stage if LH2 records it. If LH2 does not, LR3's spec either records the prompts in LR3's own record or asks for a `reading.py` settings field after LH2 merges, one writer at a time (§3) `(r3)` |\n356\t\n357\tOpen questions carried into the specs: LR1, whether the page's steps are\n358\tshown as a short Python snippet the documentation tests run or as prose with\n359\tfield names; LR2, whether `block_id` is the recommended place for the shown\n360\tsection or a new documented convention; LR3, the size of the set, and\n361\twhether precision counts a kept fact outside the gold passages as wrong, as\n362\t#226 did.\n363\t\n364\t## 11. r3: the first panel round's fixes\n365\t\n366\tThe first round ([r2 panel](../../../reviews/literature-reading-reference-r2-panel/README.md))\n367\tread r2 at SHA-256\n368\t`4960c18dfcf59c7b15b0ca0da1964ae5a4bf6c5034d43455dfb21c8cac97dee2`. Five of\n369\tsix seats succeeded; Codex blocked. Its seven prioritized fixes and their\n370\tsites in r3:\n371\t\n372\t| Fix | What r3 changes | Sites |\n373\t|---|---|---|\n374\t| fix-lr2-document-scope | the example verifies the joined attempted sections with no sidecar; LR2-C3 pins the span branch | H9, §2 LR2, LR2-C3, LR2-C5 |\n375\t| fix-gates | whole-repository `uv run ruff check` is the lint gate; the component-index check stays | Goal, H22, §4, §9 |\n376\t| fix-d7b-opt-in | D7 (b) changes default text and would amend R0.1 and LR1-C5 | §5 |\n377\t| fix-paths | `src/gnd/` prefixes | H8, H9, H11, H13, H15, H16, H21 |\n378\t| fix-lr3-existing-corpus | the regression corpus and scorer are in D1 and D4; D4's section grain; D9's prompts; interim reply and LR3 wait | component row, H24, §2 LR3, §3, D1, D4, D5, D9 |\n379\t| fix-lr1-steps | derivation failures, staging, authored fixtures, report-level field names, absolute URL from the skill, `index.md` not an LR1 home | H2, H23, H25, §2 LR1, §3, LR1-C3, LR1-C6, §5 |\n380\t| fix-lr2-pages | `index.md:11` rewritten; the LR2 test reads the pages | §2 LR2, LR2-C5 |\n381\t\n382\tRefuted on reproduction, no change: Qwen's claim that a verdict carries no\n383\t`verdict` field (the live report carries `\"verdict\": \"fail\"`; H2 now lists\n384\tit); Kimi's claim that an include resolves against the working directory (a\n385\trun from the parent folder exits 1; what is true, that the vocabulary must be\n386\tstaged beside the model, is in H2). Codex's note that `project.md` says\n387\t\"There is no component index in this repository\" is a stale line in\n388\t`project.md` itself, which its later \"Component index\" section, `AGENTS.md`\n389\tand the sibling plans contradict; the check stays, and the stale line is\n390\treported as a follow-up, not edited here."}
