+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_fgJswgrHZVqA7JrKelfhwXnp","content":"1\t# Literature host interfaces\n2\t\n3\tPlan r6, 2026-11-23, from [issue #216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216)\n4\tand [issue #215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215).\n5\t**Plan approved by the owner on 2026-11-23** ([plan-gate record](001-plan-gate.md),\n6\tr6 sha256 `2dc760e5…1528`), with every decision ruled. The full panel\n7\treviewed r4 and r5; r6 answers the second round and is not itself reviewed.\n8\tNothing is implemented, and no phase spec is approved.\n9\t\n10\t| Phase | Deliverable | State |\n11\t|---|---|---|\n12\t| LH1 | A public producer protocol in the reading example; a caller's producer drives the six stages over a caller's root, with a budget per document, caps as parameters and optional steps recorded as skipped | [draft spec](notes/phase-LH1-spec.md), waiting for its owner gate |\n13\t| LH2 | `replay()` of a live run from its own folder and the caller's root, with zero producer calls and its settings read from the run | outline in the plan |\n14\t| LH3 | Admission over a caller-named assertion entity, identified by its own handle: every attached fact row kept, the facts of followed entities kept with them, include roots admitted | outline in the plan |\n15\t| LH4 | Admission rules as data, the status `policy-refused`, and `max_targets` as an argument up to 1,024 | outline in the plan |\n16\t\n17\t[Plan](notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md). Third in the\n18\t[roadmap after 0.4.0](../../PROJECT.md#roadmap-after-040--planned-2026-11-21):\n19\tthe reporter has working workarounds for both issues.\n20\t\n21\tThree things the plan found that the outline did not say:\n22\t\n23\t- The reading loop completes only when `gnd verify` and `gnd check` exit 0.\n24\t  A caller model with a constraint over a fact type not yet read exits 2, so\n25\t  the loop as written cannot finish on such a model (plan H23, decision D16).\n26\t- `gnd judgments check` itself stops at 1,024 targets per policy. A\n27\t  `MAX_TARGETS` parameter cannot admit more than that in one call (plan H13,\n28\t  decision D11).\n29\t- The checker does not join an objectified fact type to its entity (plan\n30\t  H14). The owner ruled that admission identifies an assertion by its own\n31\t  handle and refuses an entity that objectifies a fact type (D10).\n32\t\n33\tOwner rulings so far: D6 as proposed (a budget and a stop reason per\n34\tdocument; no early end at required coverage); D9, follow entities outward\n35\tfrom an admitted assertion; D10, own handle only; D17, as proposed (the host\n36\tlists the entity types to follow, and nothing else is followed).\n37\t\n38\tPlan review: the owner selected the full GND panel (D14) on 2026-11-23. It\n39\tran over plan r4 (sha256 `6cadaa91…7cb6`): four of six reviewers succeeded,\n40\tall asking for revision, with two blocking concerns and twelve ranked fixes\n41\t([panel record](../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/README.md)).\n42\tPlan r5 applies all twelve (plan §11). For the lint conflict the owner had\n43\tthe dev-tools scripts fixed upstream (dev-tools PR 34, merged as `a29562a`),\n44\tand gnd-public is re-synced, so the whole-repository lint exits 0 again. The\n45\tLH1 spec is brought to r5. r5's own bytes are not reviewed; r5 is not\n46\tapproved. Plan r5 adds one proposed decision, D18 (the admission row bound).\n47\t\n48\tSecond round: the owner asked for it on 2026-11-23. It ran over r5\n49\t(sha256 `c1a83237…2c9b`), and five of six reviewers succeeded:\n50\t\n51\t- Gemini approved.\n52\t- Claude, Codex, Kimi and GLM asked for revision.\n53\t- Qwen timed out.\n54\t\n55\tThree concerns reached agreement:\n56\t\n57\t- LH1-C14's run at the response and roster ceilings cannot fit the retained-file ceiling.\n58\t- §3 starts LH1 at `4ad0d216`, before the lint re-sync.\n59\t- LH1-C10 misses two of the seven ceilings.\n60\t"}
