+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_PweV0gLzExDn1yjpjuu8IJwf","content":"180\tdef _constraint_verdict_line(verdict: Any, indent: str = \"  \") -> str:\n181\t    \"\"\"ONE rendering of a constraint verdict, for every surface that prints one.\n182\t\n183\t    Extracted by the phase-2 refactoring review (protocol section 8, step 5).\n184\t    There were two copies here -- the blocking and advisory arms below print the\n185\t    same three fields the same way -- and the transition arm was about to add a\n186\t    third. Three copies of a line is how a format drifts between the report a\n187\t    reader sees for a snapshot check and the one they see for a walk, over the\n188\t    same underlying verdict.\n189\t    \"\"\"\n190\t    return (\n191\t        f\"{indent}[{verdict.verdict}] {verbalize.path_segment(verdict.constraint_ref)}: \"\n192\t        f\"{verbalize.line_text(verdict.message)}\"\n193\t    )\n194\t\n195\tdef _derivation_verdict_lines(\n196\t    verdict: Any,\n197\t    indent: str = \"  \",\n198\t) -> list[str]:\n199\t    \"\"\"Render one derivation obligation and its ordered findings.\"\"\"\n200\t\n201\t    lines = [\n202\t        (\n203\t            f\"{indent}[{verdict.verdict}] \"\n204\t            f\"{verbalize.path_segment(verdict.derivation_ref)}: \"\n205\t            f\"{verbalize.line_text(verdict.message)}\"\n206\t        )\n207\t    ]\n208\t    lines.extend(\n209\t        f\"{indent}  [{finding.kind}] {verbalize.line_text(finding.message)}\"\n210\t        for finding in verdict.findings\n211\t    )\n212\t    return lines\n213\t\n214\tdef _identified_verdict_lines(\n215\t    verdict: Any, declared: Mapping[str, tuple[str, str | None, str, str | None]] | None\n216\t) -> list[str]:\n217\t    \"\"\"A constraint verdict line, named by its declared address and followed by its remedy.\n218\t\n219\t    ``declared`` maps a positional ref to (address, remedy, message, novelty)\n220\t    for ``check --rule-ids``; the message is the version-15 one, which differs\n221\t    from the report's for a failing acyclic rule (RC2), and the novelty is\n222\t    ``new`` or ``standing`` under ``--baseline`` (RC3). Without it, the line is\n223\t    the plain one.\n224\t    \"\"\"\n225\t    if declared is None or verdict.constraint_ref not in declared:\n226\t        return [_constraint_verdict_line(verdict)]\n227\t    address, remedy, message, novelty = declared[verdict.constraint_ref]\n228\t    named = verbalize.path_segment(verdict.constraint_ref)\n229\t    if address != verdict.constraint_ref:"}
