e of its pinned bytes; do not leave lane widening as the only guard for the preferred ruling.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"LR3's focused lane names no test of the regression corpus or assurance scorer it proposes to extend"},{"concern_id":"glm:r3-interim-reply-home-unreconciled","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 5, Issue reply bullet (line 268); section 10, D5 (line 351); section 3, LR2 and LR3 homes (lines 218-219)","observation":"Line 268 still says '- **Issue reply.** The close drafts it; the owner posts it.', but D5 (r3) adds 'An interim reply to #226 covering requests 3 and 2 is drafted when LR2 merges (`notes/issue-reply.md`); the owner posts it', and section 3's homes reflect only half of that: the LR2 row (line 218) lists 'docs/reference/anchors.md, docs/literature/index.md, docs/literature/commands.md, src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md, a new tests/test_lr2_quote_scope.py, docs/release-notes.md' with no issue-reply home, while notes/issue-reply.md appears only in LR3's homes (line 219). The fix that added the interim reply to D5 did not propagate it to section 5 or to LR2's homes."}],"recommendation":"Reconcile the three sites: say in section 5 that the interim reply is drafted when LR2 merges and the close finalizes it, and add notes/issue-reply.md to LR2's homes row (or state in D5 that the file is created outside any phase's homes).","relevance":"completeness","severity":"low","title":"D5's interim reply at LR2 merge has no home in LR2 and contradicts section 5's 'the close drafts it'"},{"concern_id":"glm:r3-extraction-contract-bare-path","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","location":"section 0, R0.3 (line 73); section 1, H6 (line 103)","observation":"R0.3 cites '(`extraction-contract.md:152`)' and H6 cites '`docs/guides/documents.md:62-72`; `extraction-contract.md:136-148`' with no directory, while section 3 (line 217) and section 5 (line 259) spell the same file out as 'src/gnd/skills/gnd-extract/references/extraction-contract.md'. The bare name is unambiguous at this checkout (the only such file is the packaged-skill reference, and lines 136-148 and 152 do carry the 'REPORT IT' row and the 'checker acceptance, not proof of faithfulness' sentence), but this is the same under-prefixed-citation class the round-one fix-paths fix corrected for the examples paths, left uncorrected for the skill file."}],"recommendation":"Use the full packaged-skill path 'src/gnd/skills/gnd-extract/references/extraction-contract.md' in R0.3 and H6, matching section 3 and section 5.","relevance":"completeness","severity":"low","title":"R0.3 and H6 cite extraction-contract.md without the packaged-skill path used elsewhere in r3"}],"disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"glm","schema_version":2,"summary":"Digest verified; the plan, the round-one report, the milestone README, the LR1 draft spec and every load-bearing citation were read. All seven round-one fixes resolve in r3 at their named sites. fix-lr2-document-scope: H9, section 2 LR2, LR2-C3 and LR2-C5 now describe the joined attempted sections with no sidecar, and LR2-C3's design is sound against the code (sidecar document_sha256 names the first section and the document is that section, so the digest check at anchors.py:248 passes and the span check at anchors.py:269-270 refuses with 'source span or excerpt differs'). fix-gates: the goal, H22, section 4 and section 9 name whole-repository 'uv run ruff check', which project.md:167 confirms exits 0. fix-d7b-opt-in: section 5 now says D7 (b) as written changes the default text and would amend R0.1 and LR1-C5. fix-paths: H8, H9, H11, H13, H15, H16 and H21 carry the src/gnd/examples/literature/ prefix. fix-lr3-existing-corpus: the component row retraction, H24, D1 (d), D4's section grain, D9's conditional prompts and D5's interim reply are all in. fix-lr1-steps: derivation failures (H23, LR1-C6), the staged probe (H2), authored fixtures (section 3), report-level field names (LR1-C3) and the absolute-URL skill citation (H25, section 3, section 5). fix-lr2-pages: index.md:11 is rewritten and LR2-C5's test reads the pages. Citations match this checkout: report.schema.json requires constraint_ref, constraint_type, modality, source, status, verdict, message, offending_facts and reason_code on verdicts and derivation_ref and findings on derivations; output.py:353 and :190-193 print '[fail] <constraint_ref>: <message>' with no rows; --rule-ids exists only on the check parser (commands/checking.py:904) and the verify parser refuses it; reading.py ranges 42, 93-112, 149-158, 176-193, 311-341, 390-392, 562-584 and 587-596 all show what their rows claim; the include resolves beside the model file (model/__init__.py:409-413 uses retained_root(path.parent)), so H2's staging is correct and the round-one refutation of Kimi stands; documents.md:62-72, extraction-contract.md:136-152, index.md:11 and :309-313, test_verify_cli.py:309-336 and :387, test_packaged_skills.py:101-125, redaction.py:616-633, 016-milestone-close.md:162, the six standing rules of project.md:187 and the literature-host-interfaces README's LH1/LH2 rows all match. LR1 and LR2 are implementable and testable as sections 2 and 4 write them with the section 9 lanes; LR3's wait on LH1/LH2 and its rulings is clearly gated. Three residual concerns, none blocking."},"response_salvage":{"complete":true,"declared_concern_count":3,"dropped":[],"dropped_overflow":0,"preamble_lines":0,"retained_concern_count":3,"trailing_lines":0,"transport":"jsonl"},"reviewer_id":"glm","schema_version":1,"status":"success"}],"quorum_met":true,"request":{"kind":"plan","plan":{"media_type":"text/markdown","path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md","sha256":"a1ab8a9c87e7b733eea0b42a5306