+# Augmented Physics-Informed Neural Networks (APINNs): A gating network-based soft domain decomposition methodology (2022)
+Work arXiv:2211.08939. A synthetic paraphrase written for regression testing; it is not the text of the work. This paraphrase writes the method's name as $PINN, the LaTeX-residue spelling a host extractor produced; the work itself writes APINN.
+The paper proposes $PINN, an augmented physics-informed network whose domain decomposition is soft and trainable.
+$PINN improves on XPINN by replacing its hard split into subdomains with a gate network that can be fine-tuned.
